anks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers. Each employee generates $1.1M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $211K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Park Hotels & Resorts Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.3B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $102M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 519% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.8pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 24% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Price sits 23% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.22996867870803903},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 26% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(PK) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/23/PK_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_111326014801_1794552481.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794552481.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Investors May Respond To Park Hotels & Resorts (PK) Lowered Earnings Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-pk/park-hotels-resorts/news/how-investors-may-respond-to-park-hotels-resorts-pk-lowered","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794486789.977,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.153,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Park Hotels & Resorts (PK) Could Be 2% Undervalued Following Lowered 2026 Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-pk/park-hotels-resorts/news/park-hotels-resorts-pk-could-be-2-undervalued-following-lowe","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794392885.065,"origi